<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Ali returns three months after his first visit. Since carbidopa-levodopa was increased to one and a half tablets three times a day, taken 30 minutes before meals, he is quicker with buttons and getting out of chairs, and the late-morning slowness has eased. He has had no involuntary movements, no wearing-off before doses, and no lightheadedness on standing, nausea, or sleepiness. He finished the four-week LSVT LOUD speech therapy course two months ago and practices his voice exercises each day; people hear him more easily. He has had six physical therapy sessions and now walks, rides a stationary bicycle, and does balance exercises about 150 minutes a week. He has had no falls. He has had no hallucinations. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicine change</td><td>Levodopa 150 mg three times daily before meals for twelve weeks; slowness better</td></tr><tr><td>Motor complications</td><td>No dyskinesia or wearing-off</td></tr><tr><td>Rehabilitation</td><td>LSVT LOUD course completed; six physical therapy sessions; home program about 150 minutes a week</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

