  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Parkinson&apos;s disease, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5 (G20.A1)</content>. Good response to the levodopa increase, with MDS-UPDRS Part III down from 30 to 24 and no dyskinesia. The standing blood pressure falls by 10 mmHg, short of the 20 mmHg that defines orthostatic hypotension. Timed Up and Go improved from 13 to 11 seconds with physical therapy. [S]<list><item>Continue carbidopa-levodopa 150 mg three times daily, 30 minutes before meals.</item><item>Continue the home exercise program at 150 minutes a week or more.</item><item>Stand up slowly and drink fluids through the day; report any lightheadedness.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypokinetic dysarthria with soft speech (R47.1)</content>. Louder and easier to understand after the speech therapy course. [S]<list><item>Daily voice exercises; refresher course if his voice softens again.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>MDS-UPDRS Parts III and IV and Hoehn and Yahr stage</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Part III 24, down from 30; Hoehn and Yahr 2.5; Part IV: no dyskinesia, wearing-off, or on-off</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure, supine and after 3 minutes standing</td><td>Every visit while on dopaminergic treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>126/78 mmHg supine and 116/76 mmHg at 3 minutes standing after the dose increase; no orthostatic hypotension</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dopaminergic regimen review for wearing-off, dyskinesia, and on-off</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Good response to levodopa 150 mg three times daily with no motor complications; no change</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Avoidance of dopamine-blocking drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No dopamine-blocking drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication side effects and adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No nausea, sleepiness, or missed doses; doses now taken before meals</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall query and fall-risk assessment (Timed Up and Go, pull test)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds, improved from 13; recovers after two steps on the pull test</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Psychotic symptoms (hallucinations, delusions)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Impulse-control screen (QUIP-RS)</td><td>Every visit; mandatory on a dopamine agonist</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Not asked at this visit, a deviation from the every-visit item. He is not on a dopamine agonist, and the screen at the six-month review was negative, so no impulse-control problem was missed. Corrective action: the screen is added to the standing visit checklist</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise counseling: aerobic, resistance, and balance, at least 150 minutes a week</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 150 minutes a week of walking, cycling, and balance exercises</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At diagnosis and at least yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>Planned for the preventive visit in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Diagnosis review against the MDS clinical diagnostic criteria</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Confirmed by neurology three months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 27 of 30 four months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression, anxiety, and apathy (PHQ-9)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 3 four months ago; mood good today</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep: REM sleep behavior disorder questionnaire, Epworth Sleepiness Scale, insomnia, restless legs</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No dream enactment or daytime sleepiness</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Autonomic symptoms: constipation, urinary, sexual, sweating, drooling</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No constipation or urinary symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Swallowing screen (EAT-10)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>EAT-10 2 four months ago; no choking or coughing with meals since</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and voice loudness</td><td>Yearly; speech therapy for speech change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>LSVT LOUD course completed; louder speech today</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical, occupational, and speech therapy</td><td>At diagnosis, then reassessed yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Speech therapy completed; physical therapy in progress, moving to a home program</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Genetic testing with counseling</td><td>Once, offered to every person with Parkinson&apos;s disease</td><td>Due</td><td>Offered three months ago; decision at the yearly neurology review</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dental and oral examination</td><td>Every 6 months</td><td>Due</td><td>Not yet arranged; due by six months</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Driving safety</td><td>Yearly or with a motor or cognitive change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Motor function better; review yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>To be reviewed at the preventive visit in the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine laboratory monitoring</td><td>Not required for Parkinson&apos;s disease surveillance</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>The CMID monograph calls for no routine laboratory tests; baseline blood count, chemistry, vitamin B12, and TSH were normal at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Brain MRI</td><td>If atypical parkinsonism features appear</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No atypical features; examination unchanged apart from the improvement</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Polysomnography for REM sleep behavior disorder</td><td>If REM sleep behavior disorder treatment is considered</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No dream enactment</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AGS Beers Criteria medication review</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>He is 54</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Deep brain stimulation programming review</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months after implantation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No deep brain stimulator</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Less slowness of movement after a levodopa adjustment, without dyskinesia or orthostatic hypotension, by the three-month review. Outcome by 1996-06-09: MDS-UPDRS Part III fell from 30 to 24; no dyskinesia; no orthostatic hypotension [S]</item><item>Complete a four-week intensive speech therapy course and keep up daily voice practice. Outcome by 1996-06-09: LSVT LOUD course completed; easier to hear in conversation; daily home practice continues [S]</item><item>No falls through the six-month review, with at least 150 minutes a week of exercise including balance work. In progress; target 1996-09-08 [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record his goals of care by the preventive visit. In progress; target 1996-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Dopaminergic Therapy for Motor Symptoms in Early Parkinson Disease Practice Guideline Summary: A Report of the AAN Guideline Subcommittee (2021); MDS clinical diagnostic criteria for Parkinson&apos;s disease (2015); The recommendations of a consensus panel for the screening, diagnosis, and treatment of neurogenic orthostatic hypotension and associated supine hypertension (2017); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month Parkinson&apos;s disease review in three months. Next scheduled visit 1996-09-08: six-month Parkinson&apos;s disease review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
